  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    THROWAWAY SPIKE to de-risk the hardest R4 surface before committing Phase 3. Apply a small operation set
    (built from the task-003 schema) to the CIPO corpus document (`PAT 109270W-1 - CLAIMS track changes …
    .docx`, task 002) via BOTH candidate patch engines, and produce a decision recommendation for
    FR-04/FR-11:
    - CANDIDATE A: **Docxodus** (MIT, active .NET redline engine) — does it already do split-run + w:ins/w:del
      at an offset?
    - CANDIDATE B: **build on the Open XML SDK** directly — match `w:p` by `w14:paraId` → walk runs
      accumulating text length until the offset lands in run R → `Run.Clone()`-split R preserving
      `RunProperties` → wrap inserts in `InsertedRun`(w:ins) / deletes in `DeletedRun`(w:del) with
      Author/Date/Id. Paragraph-mark deletion (merge) = `w:del` on the para-mark glyph in `w:pPr/w:rPr`.

    Prior art: `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` finding #6 (the canonical split-run recipe — mutate the OpenXml DOM,
    NEVER string-edit `document.xml`). The spike MUST land at least one INTERIOR edit at the correct
    `paraId + offset` on the CIPO doc via each engine and compare fidelity, fit, and (for Docxodus) publish-size
    delta (NFR-04). Write the recommendation to `notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md`. This is throwaway code —
    do NOT wire it into the production save path; the real engine is task 030.

    Escalation: if NEITHER engine can land an interior edit at the correct paraId+offset on the CIPO doc, STOP
    and escalate — the Phase-0 gate cannot pass on that evidence.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET engineer deep in the Open XML SDK object model (WordprocessingDocument, Run/RunProperties,
    InsertedRun/DeletedRun, w:pPr/w:rPr para-mark, revision ids) and comfortable evaluating a third-party MIT
    library (Docxodus) against a build-your-own baseline. Understands `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out purity
    (ADR-007) and the no-AI-internals rule (ADR-013), and that this spike's recommendation decides the FR-04
    engine.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A throwaway spike that applies a small task-003 operation set to the CIPO corpus doc via BOTH Docxodus and
    build-on-OpenXML-SDK, lands at least one interior edit at the correct `paraId + offset` via each (or
    records that it could not), and produces `notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md` recommending the FR-04/FR-11
    engine on fidelity-on-CIPO + fit + (if Docxodus) publish-size delta. The spike mutates the OpenXml DOM
    (never string-edits document.xml), stays `byte[]`-in/out, and injects no AI internals.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5.0/§5.6 frame the bridge as the real engineering, and the offset→run mapping + native
      w:ins/w:del at an interior location as its hardest piece — front-loaded and spiked on the CIPO doc
      BEFORE Phase 3 (design §6). The A/B is a genuine Phase-0 evaluation (spec Assumptions: "no assumption of
      which wins"): Docxodus (MIT, active) is "the one surviving real vendor option" (plan.md), vs building on
      Open-XML-SDK. Prior art finding #6 gives the canonical recipe (match paraId → walk runs → Run.Clone()
      split at offset → wrap in InsertedRun/DeletedRun; para-mark deletion via w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del; mutate the
      DOM, never string-edit). The CIPO doc is the known interior-location-422 + empty-paragraph + pre-existing
      track-changes case (task 002 manifest). This spike consumes the task-003 operation schema (the op set it
      applies) and the task-002 CIPO fixture. It is throwaway — the production engine is task 030.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">a throwaway spike project/location (e.g. under a `spike/` or a `tests/spikes/Compose/` scratch area) exercising BOTH engines — NOT wired into the production save path; deleted or archived after the decision</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/Operations/ComposeOperation.cs — the task-003 op schema the spike builds its op set from</file>
