      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md finding #6 (canonical split-run + w:ins/w:del recipe; DOM-mutation-not-string-edit; para-mark deletion via w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — EDGE-1…4 native-OOXML revision/comment wisdom to inform the OpenXML-SDK candidate (study only; the class is retired later)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md — the A/B decision + recommendation for FR-04/FR-11</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5.0, §5.6, §6</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-04, FR-11, NFR-04, Assumptions/Unresolved Questions (Docxodus adoption)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">Fidelity corpus — supplies the CIPO fixture the spike applies edits to.</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Operation schema — the op set the spike builds and applies.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-04 / FR-11">The spike MUST apply a small task-003 operation set to the CIPO doc via BOTH engines and land at least one INTERIOR edit at the correct `paraId + offset` (or record that an engine could not). Scope: interior-location placement is the acceptance target; zero write-path text-search.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / bridge-prior-art #6">MUST mutate the OpenXml DOM, NEVER string-edit `document.xml`; split runs at the offset preserving `RunProperties`; wrap in InsertedRun/DeletedRun with Author/Date/Id; para-mark deletion via `w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del`. Scope: applies to the OpenXML-SDK candidate and is the yardstick for judging Docxodus.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">The applier is `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out; NO `Microsoft.Graph` type in the spike. Scope: SPE hop is not part of the spike.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">The spike injects NO AI internals; the op set is hand-built or read from a fixture, not produced by an AI dispatch call. Scope: pure OOXML applier evaluation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-04">If Docxodus is recommended, the decision doc MUST report its BFF publish-size delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline (zero new runtime package is the default expectation). Scope: size is a decision input, not an afterthought.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This is THROWAWAY spike code — it MUST NOT be wired into the production save path. Scope: the production engine is task 030; the spike is deleted/archived after the decision.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Open XML SDK surgical patch (split-run + w:ins/w:del); Docxodus evaluation; para-mark deletion edge; byte[]-in/out purity; publish-size delta</topic>
