  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: FULL). Load bridge-prior-art finding #6, spec §FR-04/FR-11/NFR-04, and confirm the task-002 CIPO fixture + task-003 schema are available. State the Placement Justification + run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Build the op set">From the task-003 schema, construct a small operation set targeting interior locations in the CIPO doc (at least one interior insertText/replaceRange at a specific paraId+offset; include a para-mark-deletion probe if feasible).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Candidate A — Docxodus">Evaluate Docxodus: can it apply split-run + w:ins/w:del at an offset for the op set? Land the interior edit (or record the gap). Measure its publish-size delta if adopted.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Candidate B — OpenXML-SDK build">Implement the finding-#6 recipe directly on the Open XML SDK: match paraId → split run at offset → InsertedRun/DeletedRun. Land the same interior edit; probe para-mark deletion.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Compare + decide">Compare fidelity on CIPO (open the outputs in Word / verify tracked changes land correctly), fit (effort, control, edge coverage), and size (Docxodus delta). Write `notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md` with a clear FR-04/FR-11 recommendation.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Gate-evidence + escalation check">Confirm at least one engine landed an interior edit at the correct paraId+offset. If NEITHER did, STOP and escalate (Phase-0 gate cannot pass). Ensure the spike is not wired into production.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Close out">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 005 status to ✅. Record the decision + any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>NEITHER Docxodus nor build-on-OpenXML-SDK can land an interior edit at the correct `paraId + offset` on the CIPO doc — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6: the Phase-0 gate (task 006) cannot pass, and the whole cutover half is blocked on this evidence.</trigger>
    <trigger>Docxodus is otherwise preferred but its publish-size delta pushes the BFF toward the ≤60 MB ceiling (≥+5 MB single-task delta per root §10) — surface the size/fidelity tradeoff for an explicit decision rather than silently adopting it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No patch applier exists yet; the retired `DocxAnnotationWriter` text-search path is the thing being replaced. Docxodus is a candidate NEW dependency under evaluation.</existing>
    <extension>The spike itself is throwaway (not new production surface); it exists to decide whether the FR-04 engine EXTENDS the Open XML SDK we already ship or vendors Docxodus. It evaluates, it does not add permanent surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without proving the offset→run split + native w:ins/w:del on the real CIPO worst-offender before Phase 3, the hard-replace commits to an unproven engine — the exact failure mode the Phase-0 gate exists to prevent.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="spike-code">throwaway spike exercising Docxodus + OpenXML-SDK candidates on the CIPO doc (not wired into production; archived/deleted after decision)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md — the FR-04/FR-11 engine recommendation (fidelity + fit + size)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A small task-003 operation set is applied to the CIPO corpus doc via BOTH candidate engines (Docxodus and build-on-OpenXML-SDK).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At least one engine lands an INTERIOR edit at the correct `paraId + offset` on the CIPO doc with ZERO write-path text-search (or the failure is recorded and escalated).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The OpenXML-SDK candidate mutates the OpenXml DOM (never string-edits document.xml) and probes para-mark deletion via `w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/patch-engine-ab-decision.md` states a clear FR-04/FR-11 engine recommendation weighing fidelity-on-CIPO + fit + (if Docxodus) publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: the spike injects no AI internals, uses no `Microsoft.Graph` type, and is NOT wired into the production save path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 005 as ✅ and the decision + any deviation are recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Critical path: 003 → 005 → 006. This spike + task 003 + task 004 are the three green lights the Phase-0
    gate (task 006) checks. The recommendation directly seeds task 030 (the production ComposeShadowPatchEngine).
